WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.320
The history of Dota 2 is one of greatness.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.820
LD: Not yet! Sylar to fall, Liquid are doing it!

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:08.400
They're gonna take it!

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:10.540
KuroKy: I waited four f***ing years for this day.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:13.660
This time we're gonna rewrite history.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.560
Capitalist: EG might be able to do this!

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:17.480
Evil Geniuses, they're holding!

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:18.780
LD: Ravage on everyone!

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:21.420
The black hole as well! LighTofHeaveN, turns it around!

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.480
Ravage as well!

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:24.600
Stolen by Dendi, are you kidding me!?

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:25.940
TobiWan: TNC have done it!

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:27.980
The dream, the reality!

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:31.960
But it's also a history that's not exempt from the absurd,

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.380
the embarrassing,

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:34.800
and the controversial.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.620
From game ruining bugs,

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:38.780
to the biggest of professional scandals...

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:40.800
TobiWan: I cannot believe it!

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.140
Let's look back into

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:44.360
the most hilarious balancing blunders,

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:45.900
the most shocking news,

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:49.320
and the lowest points of Dota 2's storied past.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.900
Match-fixing and intentional throws are

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.300
a hazard of any competitive game and

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.080
we're kicking things off with two of the

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:04.920
the most infamous examples in Dota 2 history.

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:07.440
On June 14th 2013,

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:11.960
RoX.KiS took on zRage in an online match in StarLadder

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:13.800
Star Series sixth season.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:17.220
Despite being the favourites, RoX lost the game in

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.040
suspicious fashion with a number of

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:20.840
highly questionable engages

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:22.820
and buybacks throughout the game.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:23.620
Sheever: They actually want to try to go in with this,

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:24.760
Bzz...

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.480
He was already very low to begin with...

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:30.000
They just run in here to die!

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.840
What's up with that?

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:32.320
That's not good...

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:34.660
The surprise upset was investigated by

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.260
StarLadder officials,

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:38.540
and two days later it was determined that

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:40.320
Alexei "Solo" Berezin

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.220
had intentionally thrown the match after placing a bet

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:46.420
against his own team on egamingbets.com

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:02.420
Solo publicly apologized for throwing the match,

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:05.660
and admitted to using his girlfriend's account to place

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:08.020
a one-hundred dollar bet against his team.

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:12.020
And on June 21st, RoX removed Solo from their roster.

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:15.600
StarLadder had initially handed Solo a lifetime ban

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:16.960
for his actions,

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:21.200
but ended up reducing his ban to one
year following his public apology

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.920
and cleared up any suspicion against the organization

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:25.040
and its other players.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.860
Solo's winnings would have totaled

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:48.920
three-hundred and twenty-two dollars

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:50.880
and the community wasted no time

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:53.000
in making the number three-two-two

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.420
a popular meme throughout esports,

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:57.280
often sarcastically referenced when a

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:59.140
player is playing so badly

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:01.040
it is borderline suspicious.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:02.360
Maut: Don't do it Zai, you're too young!

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:03.480
What are you doing?!

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.600
[laughter]

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:07.860
But, a year later, a highly publicized match-fixing

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:09.520
scandal took place that ended

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:11.520
with much more dire consequences.

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:13.360
In October of 2014,

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.460
in Southeast Asia's Synergy League,

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:17.660
the heavily favoured Arrow Gaming lost to

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:20.220
Australian squad Can't Say Wips,

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:23.220
prompting an investigation by Dota 2 Lounge.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:26.120
The examination uncovered several bets

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:29.200
placed by individuals associated with the team

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.360
leading Arrow Gaming to be disqualified

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:32.300
from the tournament.

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:34.700
Further investigations uncovered that

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:36.420
the bets originated from accounts

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:39.780
belonging to the girlfriends of ddz and Lance,

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.160
resulting in the two players

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:43.800
receiving lifetime bans from the event.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.420
Soon after the investigation, Arrow Gaming protested

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:49.820
the players' innocence providing Synergy League

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:52.900
with chat logs and statements regarding the situation

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:54.320
in ddz's name.

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:56.960
However, the logs were proven to be doctored

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:58.620
and the statements false,

00:03:58.620 --> 00:03:59.760
and as a result,

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.580
Synergy League extended the bans

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:04.300
to Arrow Gaming's entire organization.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.220
As a result of the whole debacle,

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:09.340
Arrow Gaming and all of its players were removed from

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:12.660
the line-up for The Summit 2's SEA qualifiers

00:04:12.660 --> 00:04:15.160
and are still banned from Synergy League.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:18.400
Shortly after the incident ddz took to Facebook to

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:21.400
publicly apologize on behalf of the players.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.560
Admitting that they had three-two-two'd

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:25.620
and that the statements and chat logs provided

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:28.560
to Synergy League were forged by Arrow's management

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:30.680
and not written by the players.

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:34.340
A few days later Dota website 2p reported that team

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:37.680
manager Jaren Gan had threatened to sue Lance

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:40.060
and ddz for eight-thousand dollars each

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:41.420
for breach of contract

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:43.340
should they not retract their confession.

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:45.120
Arrow Gaming would eventually

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:46.840
release its entire roster.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:49.560
But that wasn't the end of it.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.680
On March 28th, 2015,

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:54.100
Valve stepped in, handing out permanent bans

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:56.440
to all former members of Arrow Gaming

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:58.140
from Valve sponsored events –

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:00.060
including the International.

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:03.200
While there are other examples of Dota 2 match-fixing,

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:05.860
and still some we might not even know about,

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:07.460
Arrow Gaming and Solo's

00:05:07.460 --> 00:05:10.460
three-to-two are among the most memorable.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:15.380
Bugs come and bugs go,

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:17.800
but some remain in infamy for just how

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:19.380
ridiculous they are.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:21.420
Of all the bugs in Dota 2's history,

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:24.460
one stands above the rest for both how broken

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:26.600
and straight-up hilarious it was.

00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:31.480
In patch 6.75 Chen's abilities received a minor tweak as

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:34.460
the ability to send allies back to base was

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:37.900
moved off Holy Persuasion and back to Test of Faith.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:41.180
But in this process, something broke in the game.

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:42.340
For some reason,

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:46.040
Holy Persuasion, the ability used to control creeps,

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:47.760
now worked on Roshan.

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:49.860
You'd think that having Roshan,

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:51.860
with his thousands of health,

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:53.920
crushing basic attacks and abilities

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:56.700
would be a bit strong to have as a pet...

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:58.420
...And you'd be right.

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:02.540
The discovery spread like wildfire

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:05.380
and pretty soon, level one heroes, towers,

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:06.560
and neutral creeps

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:09.200
were falling to Roshan's relentless attack.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:14.860
Basically, whichever team had a Chen

00:06:14.860 --> 00:06:16.860
would have free reign of the map

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:18.020
from minute one.

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:20.000
In all but the rarest of times

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:23.180
that would lead to a dominant victory.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:28.280
Within hours of the bug's discovery,

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:30.280
Valve issued a hotfix...

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:35.100
...Ending Chen's very brief reign of terror.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.160
Now, nearly five-years old

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:40.060
this bug remains one of Dota's most iconic.

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:41.820
While it generated plenty of salt

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:43.060
at the time of its release,

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:45.640
Today, you have to laugh at its absurdity.

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:56.480
The International 2014 set records for its

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:58.460
10 million dollar prize pool and with

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:01.540
that much money, teams were looking to gain every

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:02.880
advantage possible,

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:05.760
pouring hours into carefully crafting winning strategies

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:07.740
that would make them millionaires.

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:10.460
So when a Chinese news crew leaked team

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:12.320
strategies during the tournament,

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:14.320
you could imagine that some people were

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:15.460
pretty pissed.

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:22.400
The outrage stemmed from a Weibo post

00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:25.080
made by a user known as Dr.Kleiber,

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:26.580
who posted a passionate

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:28.780
open letter explaining the situation.

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:31.760
According to the post, the crew of the website Gamefy

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:33.800
made their way into Team DK's

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:36.560
off-limits game room and started rolling,

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:39.160
despite having no permission from Team DK

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:40.460
or Valve to do so.

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:42.460
Initially posted to Youku,

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:44.440
the video was translated to English

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:46.540
and submitted to Gosu Gamers,

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:48.240
spreading across the community.

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:49.960
While both videos were taken down,

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:54.120
after a furious interview by Team DK coach "71",

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:57.000
the video had spawned mirrors and copies all over

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:57.940
the internet.

00:07:57.940 --> 00:08:00.820
According to "71", the video revealed

00:08:00.820 --> 00:08:03.920
DK's core strategy and drafting ideas.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:06.060
For not just the game in question,

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:07.700
but the entire tournament.

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:22.480
To make matters worse,

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:26.100
the Weibo post also indicated that Gamefy had posted

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:29.020
a similar video on June 11th, where they

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:31.820
recorded Invictus Gaming's team conversation.

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:35.320
Thankfully, Ferrari_430 noticed the camera

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:36.580
and left the room

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:39.620
meaning not too much of IG's discussion was leaked.

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:40.820
Following the leak,

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:44.720
iceiceice joined his coach in expressing his displeasure

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:45.740
with Gamefy.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:59.680
A day after the outrage,

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:02.540
Gamefy posted an apology to their Weibo,

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:04.780
where they begged the community for forgiveness.

00:09:04.780 --> 00:09:07.800
In compliance with Valve's rules, the personnel who

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:10.320
were involved in the leak did not continue reporting

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:11.260
on the event.

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:12.820
Although Gamefy still worked

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:14.540
for the remainder of the tournament.

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:16.860
The community, upon hearing of the leak was

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:20.380
understandably furious at the journalist in question.

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:22.840
The outrage prompted Gamefy's producer

00:09:22.840 --> 00:09:24.760
to post another apology,

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:27.600
this time directly defending the "well-intentioned"

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.840
reporter from whom the leak resulted.

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:31.820
The overall impact of the Gamefy leak

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:35.260
on TI4's outcome is hard to extrapolate,

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:39.020
But it's even harder to deny its influence on Team DK,

00:09:39.020 --> 00:09:40.940
who headed into the tournament as one

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:42.040
of the clear favourites.

00:09:42.340 --> 00:09:44.500
Needless to say, it is one of the largest scale

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:46.980
leaks in Dota 2's history and remains

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:48.880
the most memorable scandal to emerge

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:50.180
from The International.

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:57.180
The term game-breaking can be thrown around loosely...

00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:59.180
Ayesee: He's gonna try it again, can he...

00:09:59.180 --> 00:10:00.720
Got him that time!

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:01.740
[crowd cheers]

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:03.280
See you in the base, Mu!

00:10:04.440 --> 00:10:05.240
Welcome home!

00:10:05.240 --> 00:10:08.200
But in Dota 2, one particular bug stands out

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:10.600
for quite literally breaking the game.

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:13.900
In patch 6.81, Vengeful Spirit received a change

00:10:13.900 --> 00:10:17.120
to her aura that would apply a damage debuff

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:18.980
to any hero that killed her.

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:20.080
Simple right?

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:23.360
Unfortunately, a bug caused the game to instantly crash

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:26.520
if the aura debuff was applied to any non-player.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:28.460
Essentially a death to creeps

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:31.420
or towers would force everyone out of the lobby.

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:33.420
The bug was exploited almost instantly,

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:37.220
much to the frustration of a large part of the community,

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:40.680
as griefers intentionally suicided to prevent themselves

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:43.340
from losing, ruining countless games.

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:45.460
To no one's surprise the issue was

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:47.460
hot-fixed by Valve within a day of its

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:50.280
discovery after massive community outcry.

00:10:50.280 --> 00:10:52.020
While many bugs have appeared since this

00:10:52.020 --> 00:10:53.900
rage inducer from 2014,

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:57.000
few have had the catastrophic consequences of

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:58.880
6.81's Venge aura.

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:05.660
While Dota has had its fair share of bad

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:07.140
tournaments in the past,

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:08.940
none have captured the community's ire

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:10.600
quite like the Shanghai Major.

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:14.980
KotLGuy: Where to begin?

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:19.220
It seemed like every hour saw a new issue arise.

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:20.700
As the days rolled on the event

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:22.620
went from rage inducing...

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:23.580
Draskyl: What?

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:27.540
ODPixel: Did they say GG?

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:29.420
Draskyl: They definitely didn't.

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:31.520
..to almost comedic in its ineptitude.

00:11:32.820 --> 00:11:35.080
[laughter]

00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:37.080
Between the wealth of production issues,

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:38.760
logistical nightmares,

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:40.320
and endless delays,

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:43.140
nothing seemed to be going right for anyone involved.

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:46.160
And that doesn't even cover all the problems,

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:48.100
such as players' keyboards going missing,

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:50.400
talent not receiving food, water or

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:52.100
transportation to the venue,

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:53.580
the laughable VIP room...

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:55.820
LD: So, they've added some chairs since

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:56.740
I last came in.

00:11:56.740 --> 00:11:58.020
Not so soundproof booths,

00:11:58.020 --> 00:11:59.940
and fans and cosplayers being

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:01.580
asked to leave the venue.

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:03.600
We could go on, but you get the idea.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:05.560
ppd: There's been so many delays and problems

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:07.940
and it really makes our game and

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:09.420
what we're doing here look bad,

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:11.440
which is unfortunate for everyone involved.

00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:14.320
Sheever: Because the production is not great...

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:16.480
We're gonna continue here with one more

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:18.900
match today though, Evil Geniuses, MVP Phoenix and

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:20.520
we're gonna go continue with that after

00:12:20.520 --> 00:12:22.640
a small break, so we'll see you soon.

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:30.960
Soon.

00:12:30.960 --> 00:12:31.460
[laughter]

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:33.720
Eventually Valve fired production company

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:36.320
Perfect World and PGL was hired

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:38.380
to salvage the rapidly sinking ship.

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:41.320
And while PGL saved the show, it was too late.

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:43.380
The Shanghai Major was already going to

00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:45.840
go down in history as one of Dota 2's

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:47.400
most embarrassing events.

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:50.120
It really is a shame that the event went so wrong

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:53.120
because against the backdrop of disaster,

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:55.700
the games were fantastic and the casters and talent

00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:57.740
poured their all into it.

00:12:57.740 --> 00:12:59.320
TobiWan: The black hole! The vac is there!

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:00.120
There's a hole!

00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:01.220
Now they go!

00:13:01.220 --> 00:13:03.200
Universe force staffs the other way to safety!

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:04.520
They can't do anything to the cleave!

00:13:04.520 --> 00:13:07.620
In from Arteezy, and that's the danger zone!

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:10.340
In some cases, pulling double or even triple

00:13:10.340 --> 00:13:12.480
shifts to make sure that the show would go on.

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:14.760
But while all that might be enough to put

00:13:14.760 --> 00:13:17.200
Shanghai on the wrong side of history,

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:20.300
it was the firing of James "2GD" Harding

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:23.520
that elevated the major to a new level of infamy.

00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:27.100
On day two, desk host 2GD was unexpectedly

00:13:27.100 --> 00:13:28.400
replaced on the panel.

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:30.580
While the change raised some eyebrows in the

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:33.900
community since 2GD was seen as an entertaining

00:13:33.900 --> 00:13:37.320
if slightly provocative host, there had been little

00:13:37.320 --> 00:13:39.380
to suggest that his off-brand style of

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:41.540
humor would be grounds to have him fired.

00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:44.000
2GD: It's not just me here to talk about the

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:46.140
dos and don'ts of Dota 2, and the cans

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:47.460
and c***s of the teams.

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:51.860
2GD: The Chinese hotel had disabled pornography.

00:13:51.860 --> 00:13:54.740
Mr. Wang's amazing wheelchaired antics

00:13:54.740 --> 00:13:55.900
were pretty amazing.

00:13:55.900 --> 00:13:58.940
WinteR: It shouldn't be "Sir" 2GD, it should be "Old" 2GD.

00:13:58.940 --> 00:13:59.480
[laughter]

00:14:00.220 --> 00:14:02.100
2GD: You can f*** off, WinteR.

00:14:02.100 --> 00:14:04.020
2GD: Cons for CDEC...

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:06.020
...they're stubborn and only have one D.

00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:07.260
[laughter]

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:09.520
But it wasn't just his firing that got the

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:12.140
community up in arms, it was the inflammatory

00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:15.200
response to the situation on Reddit by Valve

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:17.860
co-founder and president, Gabe Newell.

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:20.840
In that statement, Newell called 2GD "an ass",

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:23.480
while offering little in the way of an explanation

00:14:23.480 --> 00:14:24.660
for his dismissal.

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:26.540
2GD responded to the post suggesting

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:29.380
that he was not just removed from the panel

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:31.140
for his raunchy humor, but for a

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:34.560
history of conflict with Valve employees and producers.

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:35.440
ppd: He came in here trying to

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:37.820
be himself and, you know, you can appreciate that

00:14:37.820 --> 00:14:39.130
but him being himself

00:14:39.130 --> 00:14:40.680
just isn't what Valve wanted to be for

00:14:40.680 --> 00:14:42.880
the face of their Major and that's their call.

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:46.380
Regardless of the reasons or any past history between

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:48.920
James and Valve, the manner in which Newell and

00:14:48.920 --> 00:14:51.800
Valve handled the dismissal and the community fallout

00:14:51.800 --> 00:14:54.380
it generated has become infamous.

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:57.520
To this day, "is an ass" is a high tier meme within

00:14:57.520 --> 00:14:59.040
the Dota 2 scene.

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:02.780
Despite the subsequent Manila, Boston, and Kiev Majors

00:15:02.780 --> 00:15:05.800
all being praised for their fantastic production values,

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:08.620
the aftertaste left by the Shanghai Major

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:11.160
will never be forgotten by Dota 2 fans.

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:13.360
2GD: So let's check out some of the highlights.

00:15:17.420 --> 00:15:18.780
SyndereN: Your face is a beautiful highlight. Yep.

00:15:18.780 --> 00:15:19.840
[laughter]

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:25.280
Broken hero releases are a pitfall of any MOBA

00:15:25.280 --> 00:15:27.420
and Dota 2 owns arguably the

00:15:27.420 --> 00:15:30.780
most outrageous one of all time.

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:33.540
The introduction of Centaur Warrunner into Dota 2

00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:37.270
in October of 2012 was basically a disaster.

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:40.460
He was unkillable levels of tanky,

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:43.100
dealt ridiculous damage, and could chain stun

00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:44.700
into death with ease.

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:47.560
His opening day win rate in Dota 2 was staggering,

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:49.700
at over sixty-seven percent.

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:51.940
The hero was a complete and total nightmare

00:15:51.940 --> 00:15:53.060
to play against.

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:05.520
Part of the reason for this unheard of dominance

00:16:05.520 --> 00:16:08.540
was that as part of the port from Dota to Dota 2

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:11.100
Centaur was given a new ultimate.

00:16:11.100 --> 00:16:12.980
Instead of Great Fortitude

00:16:12.980 --> 00:16:16.080
which gave flat strength, he received Stampede,

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:18.460
a global ability on a tiny cooldown

00:16:18.460 --> 00:16:21.580
that gave all allies maximum movement speed,

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:24.500
a ridiculous stun upon contact with an enemy

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.080
and massive damage.

00:16:26.560 --> 00:16:29.320
Things were so bad that just four days later,

00:16:29.320 --> 00:16:33.600
Centaur received nerfs – specifically to Stampede.

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:36.380
More nerfs would be dealt to the hero in December,

00:16:36.380 --> 00:16:38.820
removing the stuns from both Double Edge

00:16:38.820 --> 00:16:40.000
and Stampede.

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:42.860
The hero had finally been brought back into line.

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:43.880
Needless to say,

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:46.220
the memory of Centaur stomping players

00:16:46.220 --> 00:16:49.000
into oblivion in 1v3 scenarios is pretty

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:50.360
funny in retrospect,

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:52.360
but easily makes it one of Dota 2's

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:54.180
most iconic broken updates.

00:16:57.840 --> 00:17:07.460
[laughs]

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:09.920
Hopefully we never see such a busted

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:11.780
hero release ever again.

00:17:11.780 --> 00:17:15.100
CW: Long shall my name be remembered.

00:17:19.440 --> 00:17:23.140
Since its formation in 2014, Team Secret has been

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:24.740
a hotbed of controversy.

00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:28.160
From public roster disputes to reports of a hostile

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:29.840
team environment, it seemed like

00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:32.420
for a long time Secret couldn't keep their name

00:17:32.420 --> 00:17:33.440
out of the news

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:35.100
– and not in a good way.

00:17:35.100 --> 00:17:37.860
Even going back to their inaugural roster,

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:40.400
messy break-ups have been all too frequent.

00:17:40.400 --> 00:17:43.200
From N0tail and Fly's bitter removal,

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:46.560
To w33 and MiSeRy's very public exits,

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:49.120
changing rosters has rarely been smooth

00:17:49.120 --> 00:17:51.060
sailing for captain, Puppey, and the rest

00:17:51.060 --> 00:17:52.740
of Team Secret's management.

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:54.820
Redeye: A team of superstars, as they are,

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:57.500
but yet to gel properly, perhaps.

00:17:57.660 --> 00:18:00.080
But if dramatic roster moves were the only

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:01.660
thing that they were known for,

00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:03.660
Secret would not make this list.

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:05.960
On February 16th, 2016,

00:18:05.960 --> 00:18:09.260
Team Secret's now former manager, Evany Chang,

00:18:09.260 --> 00:18:12.020
took to Twitlonger and posted a lengthy account

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:14.560
of her time with the team, where she alleged that

00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:17.120
Team Secret had missed making payments to players

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:19.160
and staff and neglected to hand out

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:21.320
tournament winnings in a timely manner.

00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:24.780
Later that year, EternalEnvy made similar accusations,

00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:26.620
alleging that he had yet to be paid

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:28.160
for a number of tournaments.

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:31.520
Additionally, stating that team director Kemal Sadikoglu

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:34.440
and captain Puppey had committed other abuses.

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:36.960
EternalEnvy claimed that the organization

00:18:36.960 --> 00:18:40.000
was secretly removing ten percent of all player winnings

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:41.600
without previous consent,

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:44.000
that players had never signed contracts

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:47.040
and that Puppey had physically bullied w33 –

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:48.320
among other accusations.

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:50.320
That same day, another former player,

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:52.420
MiSeRy, came forward.

00:18:52.420 --> 00:18:54.900
Stating that the team had failed to pay him for

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:57.460
numerous tournaments and claimed that he hadn't

00:18:57.460 --> 00:19:00.520
received agreed upon revenue from merchandise.

00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:02.960
A little more than a week later, Team Secret

00:19:02.960 --> 00:19:04.860
posted a response on their website

00:19:04.860 --> 00:19:08.580
simply titled "Update", which while not acknowledging

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:10.360
any accusations directly

00:19:10.360 --> 00:19:13.160
did admit that the organization had made mistakes

00:19:13.160 --> 00:19:14.880
attributed to its rapid growth.

00:19:15.140 --> 00:19:17.400
In March of 2017, Puppey would post

00:19:17.400 --> 00:19:19.200
his own Twitlonger

00:19:19.200 --> 00:19:21.560
announcing the departure of Sadikoglu

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:24.840
and apologizing to past members of the organization

00:19:24.840 --> 00:19:27.660
that felt that they had been wronged, further claiming

00:19:27.660 --> 00:19:30.020
that all obligations to those individuals

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:31.100
had now been met.

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:34.300
Since then, Team Secret has settled down and kept

00:19:34.300 --> 00:19:36.200
their name out of negative news,

00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:38.980
but despite consistently being a strong team that

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:41.200
has attracted serious talent over the years,

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:43.880
the organization has yet to fully rehabilitate

00:19:43.880 --> 00:19:46.780
its image in the eyes of many community members.

00:19:52.140 --> 00:19:53.300
Thanks for watching!

00:19:53.300 --> 00:19:55.720
If you want to see some more iconic esports moments

00:19:55.720 --> 00:19:57.200
subscribe to our channel

00:19:57.200 --> 00:19:59.420
and let us know what you'd like to see next.

